  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Piped CLI fragments and kernel evaluations now expose one coherent live __main__ namespace. Lexical loads, __main__ attributes, globals(), locals(), vars(), dir(), deletion, and global restoration agree across cells; magic globals initialize once; and intrinsic aliases stop lowering intrinsically after assignment, loops, definitions, imports, or deletion.",
    "risks": [
      "The lane remains based on dcc1302 while origin/main has advanced substantially; test:changed therefore expanded to 583 unrelated files and was stopped after its build phase at the integration coordinator's direction.",
      "The live namespace keeps deleted global accessors internally so functions compiled before deletion can restore the binding; the reusable __main__ proxy deliberately filters those undefined accessors from Python introspection."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Independently review the proxy invariants and intrinsic-alias invalidation before integration.",
      "Rebase or merge through the integration lane before running repository-wide validation against current origin/main."
    ]
  }
